---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const p = "font-size:15px;color:#333;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1rem;";
const h2 = "font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:1.4rem;color:#1a1a1a;margin:2rem 0 0.75rem;line-height:1.3;";
const a = "color:#1a2e1f;";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | BenefitsCheck UK"
  description="BenefitsCheck UK privacy policy. Our checkers run in your browser; this page explains the few cases where data is processed, including the PIP Answer Helper, newsletter and ads."
>
  <div style="max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 2rem;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;">
    <a href="/" style="font-size:13px;color:#1a2e1f;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;">← Back to home</a>
    <h1 style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:2.2rem;color:#1a1a1a;margin:1.5rem 0 1rem;line-height:1.2;">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p style={p}>BenefitsCheck UK is an independent website run by a UK-based sole trader. It is not part of, or endorsed by, the DWP or any government body. This page explains what information is processed when you use the site, and why. If you have a question, please use our <a href="/contact/" style={a}>contact page</a>.</p>

    <h2 style={h2}>Benefit checkers</h2>
    <p style={p}>All of our eligibility checkers run entirely in your browser. The answers you enter (such as income, age or health circumstances) are not sent to us, and we do not store them. If you close or refresh the page, they are gone.</p>

    <h2 style={h2}>PIP Answer Helper</h2>
    <p style={p}>The optional <a href="/pip-answer-helper/" style={a}>PIP Answer Helper</a> works differently. When you ask for a draft, the activity, condition and description you type are sent to our server function and on to our AI provider, Anthropic, to generate the draft. Because this can include information about your health, we only send it after you tick the consent box, and we ask you not to include your name or anything else that identifies you.</p>
    <p style={p}>We do not save your description or the draft. Anthropic processes the text to produce the draft under its commercial API terms; it does not use API content to train its models by default and keeps it only for a limited period for safety and abuse monitoring. See <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" style={a}>Anthropic's privacy policy</a> for details.</p>
    <p style={p}>To prevent misuse, we count how many drafts are requested using a random session ID and your IP address. These counters are held by our database provider, Upstash (UK region), and expire automatically after 24 hours. They do not contain anything you typed.</p>

    <h2 style={h2}>Newsletter</h2>
    <p style={p}>If you sign up to our newsletter, your email address is held by our email provider, Buttondown, so we can send you updates. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in every email, and we will delete your address on request.</p>

    <h2 style={h2}>Contact form</h2>
    <p style={p}>If you contact us, we use the details you send only to reply to you. Please don't send personal benefit or health details unless they are needed to answer your question.</p>

    <h2 style={h2}>Advertising and cookies</h2>
    <p style={p}>This site uses Google AdSense to show advertisements, which helps keep the site free. Google and its partners may use cookies to show ads, and where required you will be asked for your consent first. You can change your choices at any time, and you can opt out of personalised advertising through <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" style={a}>Google's Ad Settings</a>.</p>
    <p style={p}>Our hosting provider, Netlify, keeps standard server logs (such as IP addresses and pages requested) for security and to keep the site running.</p>

    <h2 style={h2}>Your rights</h2>
    <p style={p}>You have the right to ask what personal data we hold about you, and to ask us to correct or delete it. If you are unhappy with how we handle your information, you can complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" style={a}>Information Commissioner's Office</a>.</p>

    <p style="font-size:13px;color:#888;margin-top:2rem;">Last updated: November 2026</p>
  </div>
</Base>
